PS5 fan: hwmon driver (meower 883eef9 by Armandas Kvietkus + upstream #66 Pro fix by Borchev), ported

drivers/ps5/fan.c + autoservo_param.h from upstream #66 (same as rmux's meower hwmon curve
driver, plus #66's PS5 Pro fix: the Pro hands the MainSoC zone over in manual mode, which made
the driver fail to probe; it's returned to firmware auto). Kconfig: X86_PS5 also selects HWMON.
ps5.h: ps5_is_viola() (0x13da and 0x13dc).

Adapted for this image (upstream defaults to its own kernel fan curve at boot):
 - pwm1_enable 2 = the console's own firmware fan control, the DEFAULT (what every release so
   far did); 3 = the kernel's curve (pwm1_auto_point*), opt-in; 0 full, 1 manual as upstream
 - target_temp on the platform device (/sys/bus/platform/devices/ps5-fan/target_temp) kept, as
   the old driver had it: ps5-perf's FAN_TARGET and the hwcon plugin write it
 - after an emergency (max fan) the driver returns to firmware control, not the curve
hwmon also exposes temp1..temp5 (fan zones + ICC sensor 18 as Local4), fan1_input, pwm1.
